// Signing identity, which is per-developer and therefore not committed.
//
// This matters more here than in most projects. macOS keys TCC permission
// grants to the code signature, so under ad-hoc signing every rebuild silently
// invalidates the Screen Recording grant while the app continues to *look*
// enabled in System Settings. Setting a team gives the binary a stable identity,
// which is what makes rebuilding from the terminal safe.
//
// To build with your own: copy Local.xcconfig.example to Local.xcconfig and put
// your team ID in it. Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab does the same thing.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Optional, so a clone with no Local.xcconfig builds without a missing-file
// warning. Automatic signing will then ask for a team, which is the correct
// prompt rather than a confusing failure against somebody else's account.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
